## Idea

Introduce a new optional, repeatable header `Tags:` carrying revocable
triage labels (`needs-human`, `deferred`, `post-conference`, …).
Triage state is **not** Status — Status (per 0012) is closed/not-closed,
terminal and one-way. Triage labels are revocable annotations on
otherwise-open tickets.

```
%erg v1
Title: ...
Tags: needs-human          # repeatable, optional
Tags: deferred
...
```

## Why a separate mechanism

The asymmetry is deliberate:

| Concern | Mechanism | Revocable? | Carries reason? |
|---|---|---|---|
| Closed-ness | 0012's path test OR `Closed: <reason>` marker | No (one-way gate) | Yes (in the marker value) |
| Triage labels | `Tags:` header, repeatable, closed value set | Yes (delete the line) | No (label is the message) |

`Closed:` is terminal and semantic — the value names the reason (PR,
supersession, abandonment). `needs-human` is queue state — when a
human picks the ticket up, the tag is removed and the ticket flows
back into `erg ready`. Path-based or marker-based schemes for
`needs-human` would force file moves or marker-deletion ceremonies for
every revocation, which is the wrong shape.

## Composition with 0012 and 0013

- **0012 must land first** to free up the cognitive space (no Status
  enum in play), and to ensure there's only one closed/not-closed
  mechanism before we add a second triage mechanism. After 0012, the
  spec has zero state in headers; this ticket adds one revocable layer
  back, deliberately and minimally.
- **0013 is independent.** `.wip` is a parallel concern (concurrency,
  not triage). 0015 doesn't touch it.
- **0008 (erg pick) is the consumer.** Its 3-strikes path becomes:
  append `Tags: needs-human` instead of mutating Status. Its exclusion
  filter becomes: skip tickets carrying any tag in the "skip" subset.

## Spec change (rules/tickets.md)

Add a row to the headers table:

| Header | Required | Type | Values |
|--------|----------|------|--------|
| `Tags` | no | enum | (closed value set, see below) |

Repeatable: one `Tags:` line per label.

Closed value set (initial v1.x):
- `needs-human` — agent surrendered; awaiting human triage.
- `deferred` — work parked, comes back later.
- `post-talk` — defer until after a specific talk/event.
- `post-conference` — defer until after a specific conference/event.

Adding a label is appending a `Tags:` line. Removing a label is
deleting that line. The validator rejects unknown values. Extending
the set is a v1.x bump (no breakage), since unknown values fail
validation rather than parsing silently.

## Validator (tickets/tools/go/main.go)

- Accept `Tags` as a known optional repeatable header.
- Validate each value against the closed set (reject unknown).
- Expose the parsed tags via the `Erg` struct so consumers can read
  them.

## `erg ready`

- Exclude any ticket carrying a tag in the "skip" subset
  (`needs-human`, `deferred`, `post-talk`, `post-conference` — i.e.
  the entire current set, since each implies "not ready").
- JSON output: emit a `tags` array (always present, possibly empty)
  for each open ticket candidate, including blocked ones.

## `erg pick` (consumed by 0008)

- 3-strikes path: append `Tags: needs-human` and the
  `sweep-skip: three-strikes` log line. **No Status mutation** —
  there is no Status to mutate after 0012 lands.
- Exclusion filter: same skip subset as `erg ready`.
- JSON output: include `tags` per candidate (informational; pick's
  own filter already removes skip-tagged tickets).

## Out of scope

- Free-form tagging. Values are a closed set in v1; new triage
  situations require a v1.x bump.
- Tag-with-reason. If a label needs a reason ("deferred until X"),
  put the reason in a log line, not in the header value. Keeps the
  enum closed.
- Reviving the Status enum under another name. `Tags:` is for
  *additional* labels, not a replacement for the closed/not-closed
  axis 0012 establishes.

## Migration

No existing tickets carry these tags; nothing to migrate. The
validator change is additive (new optional header). Old tickets
without `Tags:` continue to validate.

## Sequencing

1. 0013 — drop `.wip`/claim/release (proposed in PR #10).
2. 0012 — drop Status enum (open design questions; this proposal
   assumes 0012 is accepted).
3. **0015 — this ticket.** Implement after 0012 lands.
4. 0014 — modularize (independent; can land in parallel with any of
   the above).
5. 0008 — `erg pick` lands on top of 0014 + 0015.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `rules/tickets.md` documents `Tags:` header with closed value set
- [ ] Validator accepts `Tags:` and rejects unknown values
- [ ] `Erg` struct exposes parsed tags
- [ ] `erg ready` excludes skip-tagged tickets and emits `tags` in JSON
- [ ] `erg pick` 3-strikes appends `Tags: needs-human` (no Status mutation)
- [ ] Tests cover: valid tag, unknown tag rejected, skip-tag exclusion
      in ready, tag round-trip
